@.str.s6258 = private unnamed_addr constant [1960 x i8] c"\0A    Usage:\0A\0A    Project commands -- these read build.ums, found at or above the\0A    working directory, and write to .prismio/build/<profile>/:\0A      prismio init [name]                        start a project here, or in a new directory\0A      prismio build [--release] [target...]      build every target, or the ones named\0A      prismio run [--release] [target] [-- args...]\0A                                                 build, then run the executable target\0A      prismio test [--release] [test...]         build and run the test targets\0A      prismio clean [--release]                  remove this profile's build output\0A      prismio <name> [args...]                   run a command the manifest declares\0A\0A    Single-file commands -- these name a source and need no manifest:\0A      prismio build <source.psm> [-o output] [-g] [-O0..-O3] [--overflow-checks]\0A                    [--target <triple>] [--sysroot <sdk>]\0A      prismio run <source.psm> [-o output] [-g] [--overflow-checks] [--jit]\0A                    [-- args...]\0A      prismio check <source.psm> [--diagnostic-format=json]\0A                    [--overlay <file.psm> <text>] [--module <name>]\0A\0A      prismio --version            which compiler, LLVM and standard library\0A      prismio --help-all           every command and flag, the compiler-development ones too\0A\0A          The debug profile builds with -g and --overflow-checks; --release\0A          builds optimised with neither. A manifest can change either in a\0A          `profiles` block.\0A\0A          -g emits DWARF, so the program can be run under lldb or gdb, and\0A          drops the object step to -O0: a variable folded into a register is a\0A          variable a debugger cannot show you.\0A\0A          --target takes an LLVM target triple -- x86_64-apple-macos,\0A          aarch64-linux-android, x86_64-pc-windows-msvc,\0A          x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu